** After opener's other rebids at the one-level response

Opener's lower-ranking new suit at the two level (12--18) is passed with 6--9
and a fit for it, preferred back to opener's first suit (6--10), raised to
game-forcing strength with notrump (2NT 11--12 invites, 3NT 13+); a reverse or
jump shift (16+) is answered with a raise of the new suit with four cards, 2NT
with 6--9 and 3NT with 10+; opposite the 2NT rebid (18--19) responder bids a
six-card major at game, and otherwise 3NT.

