** After a two-over-one response

The two-over-one response (10+) promises another bid: after opener's minimum
rebid of his suit responder raises a major with two-card support (game with
13+, the three-level invitation with 10--12), bids notrump by strength or
rebids a six-card suit; after any other rebid (a new suit, a raise, a jump,
2NT), the partnership is in a game-forcing or near-game auction and responder
places it: game in opener's major with three-card support, otherwise 3NT
(with 12+ opposite 2NT, passing a minimum).

#CUT after-2over1-major
